Package: prCGGM
Type: Package
Title: Prior-Informed Conditional Gaussian Graphical Models
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Alessia", "Mapelli", email = "alessia.mapelli@polimi.it",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Francesca", "Ieva", role = "ths"),
    person("Politecnico di Milano", role = "cph")
    )
Description: Estimates Gaussian graphical models whose mean and precision matrix
    depend linearly on sample-level covariates, while integrating prior
    knowledge on the network structure. A typical application is the
    reconstruction of personalised protein-protein interaction networks from
    proteomics data, with clinical or demographic variables as covariates and
    interaction confidence scores from the 'STRING' database as prior
    knowledge. Prior knowledge enters through a weighted sparse-group lasso
    penalty that is applied only to the
    population-level network, so that covariate-specific changes remain
    entirely data-driven. Node-wise regressions are fitted with 'glmnet' and
    'sparsegl'; the penalty and the structural hyperparameters are selected
    per node by the Bayesian information criterion of the least-squares
    refit (or, optionally, by its extended version, cross-validation or
    stability selection), the selected edges
    are refitted by least squares, and
    personalised networks can be predicted for new individuals from their
    covariates. Estimation runs sequentially, in
    parallel on a single machine, or as 'SLURM' array jobs on computing
    clusters. The method is described in Mapelli et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2606.31805>.
